From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 05:10:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(web): Settings search entry and session fake for the
 terminal extra-keys row

The carried extra-keys row does not pass the web tests on current main:

- Its Extra keys row select in Settings > Appearance is left out of the
  Settings search catalog and exempted in the unowned-controls baseline
  instead. Settings search cannot find it, and the rendered-page guard
  (settingsPageAudit.test.tsx: every control has an owner in the catalog)
  fails on it.
- The terminal view now calls setInputTransform on every session it
  attaches, which the fake session in terminalPaneMoves.lifecycle.test.tsx
  lacks, so that file ends with unhandled rejections.

The select now belongs to a catalog entry, `terminal-extra-keys`: the row
takes its label, description and choices from it, search finds it by
"terminal", "touch" or a key name, and the three baseline exemptions go.
The fake session gains the method.

Not proposed upstream yet: both changes belong in the carried pull request,
https://github.com/omnigent-ai/omnigent/pull/6136, whose own CI fails on
them; drop this copy with the carried patch once that merges.

Docs: none (the setting is documented with the extra-keys row; this only lets Settings search find it)
Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
